    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Dictionary encoding: maps frequent strings to compact integer codes.</para>
<para>The codec is built from a training corpus (a list of strings). Strings that appear at least min_frequency times are assigned codes starting at 0. All other strings receive the sentinel code kMissCode. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
